{%- doc -%}
  A label at one end of a card and its value at the other (Figma: Standart Product
  Page → the three lines inside Estimated Shipping).

  The two halves are set differently — the label smaller and grey, the value black
  and a shade heavier — which is what makes the value read as the answer.

  It lives in the kit rather than in the block because two callers draw it: the
  [_ui-product-detail-row] block, which is what a merchant arranges in the theme
  editor, and [_ui-product-panel], which draws one of these per `detail_row`
  metaobject entry when a product carries its own lines. One markup, so the two
  paths cannot drift.

  @param {string} [label] - The wording at the start.
  @param {string} [value] - The answer, pushed to the far end.
  @param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes.
  @param {string} [attributes] - Extra HTML attributes to render on the element.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-detail-line', label: 'Ships from', value: 'Made fresh, ships within 24 hrs' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- if label != blank or value != blank -%}
  <div
    class="ui-detail-line{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
    {%- if attributes != blank %} {{ attributes }}{% endif -%}
  >
    {%- if label != blank -%}
      <span class="ui-detail-line__label">{{ label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if value != blank -%}
      <span class="ui-detail-line__value">{{ value }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-detail-line {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 4px 16px;
  }

  .ui-detail-line__label {
    color: var(--ui-color-gray);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-body-weight);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  /*
   * Pushed to the far end whether or not the line has a label, so a value-only line
   * stays in column with the ones above it instead of starting at the left.
   */
  .ui-detail-line__value {
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    color: var(--ui-color-black);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-emphasis);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-emphasis-weight);
    line-height: var(--ui-line-height);
    text-align: end;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
